overview": "Northeast Pennsylvania's 8th District pairs a Republican-leaning electorate (R+4) with a Democratic-favorable national environment, making this a genuine battleground. First-term Representative Rob Bresnahan faces Scranton Mayor Paige Cognetti in a race most analysts call a Tossup; three rating services (FPO, Silver Bulletin, Split Ticket) lean toward a Democratic flip. Betting markets put Cognetti's chances near two-thirds.\n\nFundraising is roughly even, though Cognetti holds a cash edge ($3.4M to $2.6M) and outside groups, including Giffords PAC, are spending against Bresnahan, whose stock-trading record has drawn sustained scrutiny and dueling ad wars with Cognetti's own record. The three available polls, all from Democratic-leaning firms and the newest from June, show narrow Cognetti leads and carry limited weight. The forecast treats this as a close contest with a slight Democratic tilt, pending the late-October debate and fresher polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5916, "margin": 1.42}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6449, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6453, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6734, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.617, "margin": 2.4}]}